IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part5-ministers`

-- Tests for ss 19 to 19E. Expected values are written from the text. What a table result means on a given day depends on the
-- Administrative Arrangements Order, which is outside the text: the results are descriptions, and the tests assert the description
-- the table row names.

§ `Section 19: references to Ministers`

-- Item 1: "the Minister", without identifying the Minister.
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by the expression the Minister, without identifying the Minister` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the provision on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by the expression the Minister, without identifying the Minister` TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the provision on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
-- Item 2: by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a law (paragraph (a) the Act or a provision of it, paragraph (b) another Act: same result).
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a law` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering that law on the relevant day, in relation to the relevant matter`
-- Item 3(a) and (c): the Minister referred to by title administered the provision when it commenced or the reference was inserted.
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by title, even if that title no longer exists` TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, identified by item 1`, `any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Minister is responsible on the relevant day`
-- Item 3(b) and (c): (a) does not apply.
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by title, even if that title no longer exists` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Minister currently identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`, `any other Minister administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Minister is responsible on the relevant day`
-- Item 4: by describing a matter.
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference means` `by describing a matter for which the Minister is responsible` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
-- (2) An Administrative Arrangements Order or a substituted reference order, as in force on the relevant day or any earlier day, may be used.
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Minister is referred to` `an Administrative Arrangements Order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Minister is referred to` `a substituted reference order under section 19B` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An order not in force on the relevant day or an earlier day: the subsection does not say it may be used.
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Minister is referred to` `an Administrative Arrangements Order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Instruments including the following": any other instrument is not decided by the subsection.
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Minister is referred to` `any other instrument` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) Where the provision is taken to require a thing to be done by or in relation to any one of 2 or more Ministers, it is not required of more than one in a case.
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the thing must be done in a particular case` 2 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the thing must be done in a particular case` 5 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the thing must be done in a particular case` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the thing must be done in a particular case` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) Acting Ministers.
#ASSERT `a reference to a Minister is taken to include` `the Minister`
#ASSERT `a reference to a Minister is taken to include` `a Minister for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister`
#ASSERT `a reference to a Minister is taken to include` `a member of the Executive Council for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister`
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to a Minister is taken to include` `anyone else`)

§ `Section 19A: references to Departments`

#ASSERT `the Departments a reference means` `by the expression the Department, without identifying the Department` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter`
-- Example: "the Secretary of the Department" with no Department identified: under item 1 the Department administered by the Minister who administers the provision in relation to the relevant matter and that deals with that matter.
#ASSERT `the Departments a reference means` `by the expression the Department, without identifying the Department` TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering that provision in relation to the relevant matter, and that deals with that matter`
#ASSERT `the Departments a reference means` `by title, even if that title no longer exists` TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Department identified by item 1`, `any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Department is responsible on the relevant day`
#ASSERT `the Departments a reference means` `by title, even if that title no longer exists` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth identified by the title, or by a substituted reference order under section 19B`, `any other Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the matters for which that Department is responsible on the relevant day`
#ASSERT `the Departments a reference means` `by describing a matter for which the Department is responsible` FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Department is identified` `an Administrative Arrangements Order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Department is identified` `a substituted reference order under section 19B` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Department is identified` `a substituted reference order under section 19B` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which Department is identified` `any other instrument` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 19B: substituted reference orders`

-- (1) The section applies if a provision refers to an authority and one of the four things happens.
#ASSERT `section 19B applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19B applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19B applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19B applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 19B applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 19B applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (2) and (6) The Governor-General may make an order in those cases, but not only because an authority is abolished and another of the same type and name is established at once.
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The Note to (6): a change in matters dealt with, or a reference no longer appropriate, still allows an order.
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- A change of name or title alone is not within (6).
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor-General may make a substituted reference order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (3) The day specified may be a day before the order is made.
`the order made on 1 March 2026` MEANS Date 1 3 2026
`the day specified, 1 January 2026` MEANS Date 1 1 2026
`the day specified, 1 April 2026` MEANS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day on and after which the order has effect` `the day specified, 1 January 2026` `the order made on 1 March 2026` EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT `the day on and after which the order has effect` `the day specified, 1 April 2026` `the order made on 1 March 2026` EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
-- (2) "on and after a day specified": in effect on and after the specified day, not before it.
#ASSERT `the order is in effect on` (Date 1 1 2026) `the order specifies the day` `the day specified, 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `the order is in effect on` (Date 1 2 2026) `the order specifies the day` `the day specified, 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`the order is in effect on` (Date 31 12 2025) `the order specifies the day` `the day specified, 1 January 2026`)
-- (4) and (5)
#ASSERT `has effect according to its terms` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has effect according to its terms` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is a legislative instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a legislative instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7) The kinds of authority.
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19B` `a Minister`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19B` `a Department of State of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19B` `any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19B` `an office, including an APS employee's office and any other appointment or position, or the holder of an office`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an authority within section 19B` `something else`)

§ `Section 19C: references to authorities in Commonwealth agreements`

#ASSERT `section 19C applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19C applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19C applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 19C applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 19C applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 19C applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (2) The table.
#ASSERT `the authorities an agreement is taken to refer to` `a Minister` EQUALS LIST `the Minister, or any of the Ministers, administering the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
#ASSERT `the authorities an agreement is taken to refer to` `a Department` EQUALS LIST `the Department of State of the Commonwealth that deals with the relevant matter on the relevant day`
#ASSERT `the authorities an agreement is taken to refer to` `any other authority` EQUALS LIST `an authority (including the relevant authority) exercising the powers, or performing the functions, of the relevant authority on the relevant day`, `an authority (including the relevant authority) determined under subsection (4)`
-- (3)
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which authority is taken to be referred to` `an Administrative Arrangements Order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which authority is taken to be referred to` `a substituted reference order under section 19B` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `may be used to work out which authority is taken to be referred to` `any other instrument` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) The Minister administering the Department that deals with the matter may determine by notifiable instrument.
#ASSERT `is a determination for the purposes of item 3` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is a determination for the purposes of item 3` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a determination for the purposes of item 3` FALSE TRUE)
-- (5)
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the agreement requires the thing to be done in a particular case` 3 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the agreement requires the thing to be done in a particular case` 2 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the most Ministers by or in relation to whom the agreement requires the thing to be done in a particular case` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6)
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19C` `a Minister`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19C` `a Department of State of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19C` `any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19C` `an office, including an APS employee's office and any other appointment or position, or the holder of an office`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an authority within section 19C` `something else`)

§ `Section 19D: saving the validity of acts done by authorities`

-- (3) A machinery of government change occurs when any of the four things applies.
#ASSERT `a machinery of government change occurs` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `a machinery of government change occurs` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `a machinery of government change occurs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a machinery of government change occurs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a machinery of government change occurs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1), (2), (4) Each of grounds (a), (b), (c), with the mistaken belief, under an Act, an agreement or another authorisation.
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on another authority` TRUE TRUE `an Act or legislative instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on the same authority under another name or title` TRUE TRUE `an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Commonwealth` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is no longer conferred or imposed on any authority` TRUE TRUE `any other authorisation under a law of the Commonwealth` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2) Without the reasonable, but mistaken, belief the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on another authority` TRUE FALSE `an Act or legislative instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No machinery of government change.
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on another authority` FALSE TRUE `an Act or legislative instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A ground the subsection does not list; a source it does not list.
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `some other ground` TRUE TRUE `an Act or legislative instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the purported exercise is not invalid merely because of the change` `the power, function or duty is conferred or imposed on another authority` TRUE TRUE `some other source` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19D` `a Minister`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19D` `a Department of State of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19D` `any other Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act 1999`
#ASSERT `is an authority within section 19D` `an office, including an APS employee's office and any other appointment or position, or the holder of an office`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an authority within section 19D` `something else`)

§ `Section 19E: validity of acts done by Ministers`

#ASSERT `the exercise is not invalid merely because the power is conferred on the other Minister` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A Minister who exercises a power conferred on a Minister (not another one), or no purported exercise: the section says nothing.
#ASSERT `the exercise is not invalid merely because the power is conferred on the other Minister` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise is not invalid merely because the power is conferred on the other Minister` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
